      "writtenOn": "2024-08-28T15:21:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, yes it does.  \n\nThis intended to highlight this result code effectively `union`s both types of results into a single u16.  The source and sink are aware of it which is why it mostly works.  \n\nHowever,If a `L2CAP_CONN` is sourced and incorrectly sinked as a `LE_RESULT` that could be a problem, but for that several of the underlying values actually overlap correctly.\n\nThis is done due to the limitations of passing around a single connection info for both le and classic channel state machines.\n\nFuture revisions could address this by breaking them out into separate fields, or use a proper class structure to allow the language to provide this feature.\n\nThere are other statuses and fields that are intermingled with contextual required uint_t elsewhere too. (L2CAP_CFG, l2cap error callback, etc)",
      "parentUuid": "8874b5b4_cb241346",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 698,
        "startChar": 38,
        "endLine": 698,
        "endChar": 49
